id: pm-web-5ll5
title: Restore production audit after the body-parser compressed-request advisory
description: "Full browser-baseline release gate passed 830 tests and 2 capacity checks, then failed the production audit on locked body-parser 2.3.0 (GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828). Refresh body-parser and its required transitive minimum versions within the declared dependency ranges. Companion to pm-web-12wg; this does not claim hosted remediation or deployment."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,dependencies,security
created_at: "2026-10-24T05:41:14.727Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T05:43:33.311Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Production audit reports no vulnerabilities; lockfile change is limited to the compatible body-parser update; final PR CI passes npm and Bun release gates.
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T05:42:11.114Z",codex-agent,"CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/40066509482 failed only at the production audit after Node 26 passed 830/830 tests and 2/2 capacity checks. Advisory https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828 names body-parser 2.4.0 as patched. Express 5.3.0 declares body-parser ^2.3.0, so npm update body-parser selects 2.4.0 compatibly. Its required minimum versions also update iconv-lite 0.7.2 to 0.7.3 and qs 6.16.0 to 6.16.1; those are the only three changed lock entries. Direct manifests and SDK pins are unchanged. Next: lock-only audit revert proof, linked audit and targeted baseline tests, then final CI."
  "2026-10-24T05:43:31.923Z",codex-agent,"Lock-only revert proof: restored the prior package-lock.json while leaving the installed packages and audit script/policy unchanged, then npm run audit:prod exited 1 and reported GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828. Restored the updated lock byte-for-byte and ran the linked pm test --run --progress: npm run audit:prod passed with found 0 vulnerabilities. Browser-build-tree remains 8/8 and workflow-security 7/7 through the linked pm runner. The earlier CI npm gate ran 830/830 tests on both Node 22 and 26 but failed the audit; it does not satisfy the full-gate or browser acceptance requirements. Final exact-head npm/Bun and browser outcomes will be linked from PR 250 before handoff."
